WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.840
- We've seen tons of lawsuits being filed

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.450
with headline-grabbing
numbers being filed for say,

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:05.390
billions of dollars.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.360
The billion dollar lawsuit from Dominion,

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.210
or billions of dollars being sought

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.510
from Facebook and Google.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.790
But here's a secret
that only lawyers know,

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.340
that number is largely BS.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.630
The thing is, the plaintiff can put

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.350
whatever allegations they
want into the complaint

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.660
and the number that they
seek at the very end

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.930
of the complaints, the prayer for relief

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.740
is going to have a large number.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.220
Often, if you're launching
a lawsuit that has as much

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.750
of a PR component as it
does an actual legal basis,

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.760
then you're gonna want
to grab some headlines.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.490
And a lot of these
lawsuits have done that.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.950
That doesn't mean that they're entitled

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.240
to that amount of money, doesn't mean that

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.980
they're going to be awarded
that amount of money

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.460
from the judge or the jury.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.430
It just means that a plaintiff's lawyer

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.536
wants to cover their bases

00:00:44.536 --> 00:00:46.930
and they want to make sure
that they're not hamstrung

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.600
by seeking a small amount up front,

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.872
so they will put basically
any number that they want

00:00:50.872 --> 00:00:52.530
at the end of the complaint.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.580
So just remember that next
time you see a lawsuit

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.160
that is seeking billions of
dollars from someone else,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.410
that number is largely made up.

